        "PMC6175879::web::010::the_role_of_phase_boundary_in_second_pha",
        "PMC6687781::web::000::abstract"
      ],
      "same_system": "yes"
    },
    {
      "text": "The untreated eutectic HEA has limited room-temperature tensile ductility and exhibits brittle failure.",
      "field": "baseline",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The lamellar phase boundaries in the starting AlCoCrFeNi eutectic HEA are semi-coherent.",
      "field": "baseline",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "entailed",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC6175879::web::010::the_role_of_phase_boundary_in_second_pha"
      ],
      "same_system": "yes"
    },
    {
      "text": "Dislocation pile-ups at internal lamellar boundaries create local stress concentrations that cause microcracking and brittle or catastrophic failure.",
      "field": "material_initial_state",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The proposed intervention is approximately 70% cryo-rolling at liquid-nitrogen temperature followed by annealing at about 600 °C for 5–10 minutes in an inert atmosphere.",
      "field": "conditions",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC5818523::web::011::discussion",
        "PMC6687781::web::000::abstract"
      ],
      "same_system": "yes"
    },
    {
      "text": "Tight control of the anneal can avoid full recrystallization and excessive grain growth.",
      "field": "conditions",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Cryo-rolling followed by controlled annealing will refine the dual-phase lamellar architecture and produce ultrafine lamellae.",
      "field": "hypothesis",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC5818523::web::011::discussion",
        "PMC6687781::web::000::abstract"
      ],
      "same_system": "yes"
    },
    {
      "text": "The treatment will create a gradated or heterogeneous architecture containing structurally distinct fine and coarse regions.",
      "field": "structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "entailed",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC5818523::web::011::discussion",
        "PMC6687781::web::000::abstract"
      ],
      "same_system": "yes"
    },
    {
      "text": "The treatment will produce partially recovered, softened interlamellar boundaries.",
      "field": "structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC5818523::web::011::discussion"
      ],
      "same_system": "yes"
    },
    {
      "text": "Cryo-rolling introduces a high density of dislocations.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC5818523::web::011::discussion",
        "PMC6687781::web::000::abstract"
      ],
      "same_system": "yes"
    },
    {
      "text": "Cryo-rolling refines the interlamellar spacing.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Annealing after cryo-rolling promotes limited recovery and partial recrystallization at phase boundaries.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC5818523::web::011::discussion"
      ],
      "same_system": "yes"
    },
    {
      "text": "Recovered or softened interlamellar boundaries will reduce dislocation pile-ups and associated local stress concentrations.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The modified microstructure will distribute plastic deformation more homogeneously across the phases.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC6175879::web::010::the_role_of_phase_boundary_in_second_pha"
      ],
      "same_system": "yes"
    },
    {
      "text": "More homogeneous plastic deformation and reduced local stress concentrations will inhibit catastrophic microcrack initiation.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The treatment will significantly improve room-temperature tensile ductility, potentially to more than 20% elongation.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The treatment will maintain or increase yield strength relative to the untreated alloy.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC5818523::web::011::discussion",
        "PMC6687781::web::000::abstract"
      ],
      "same_system": "yes"
    },
    {
      "text": "The proposed benefits apply under quasi-static tensile loading at room temperature.",
      "field": "boundary",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
